<title>UK: UK's Clarke says to double air passenger duty.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says to double air passenger duty.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said he would double duties on air passengers</p>
<p>&quot;Air travel has also been undertaxed because it has proved difficult to get international agreement to tax its fuel,&quot; he told Parliament in his budget speech for 1997.8.</p>
<p>&quot;The rates of air passenger duty are to be increased. The 5 stg rate on flights to most European countires will be increased to 10 stg, and the 10 stg rate on flights to the rest of the world will be increased to 20 stg,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>The increases would not take effect until November 1 1997, to give tour operators time to reflect the new rates in prices published in holiday brochures, he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
